WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.950
Welcome to DBL Group's TalentHub! You are
at the centre of the whole hiring process,

2
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.320
and the last signature on
every requisition is yours.

3
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:15.160
In this video we'll see how to set who
raises requisitions and who approves them,

4
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:20.360
how to start recruitment, and how to send
the selected candidates to the board.

5
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.000
Let's get started!

6
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:28.230
The menu has the most for you.
Under Recruitment: Requisitions,

7
00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:33.958
Candidates, Talent Bank,
Approval Sheets, Medical Requests.

8
00:00:34.078 --> 00:00:39.710
Under Configuration:
Unit Config, Approval Paths,

9
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:46.390
AI Settings, Board Groups, AI Proficiency
Bank. We will take them one by one.

10
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.830
The role is group-wide, for every unit,
granted on Access Control by a super user.

11
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.380
Inside the system it
is called Corporate HR;

12
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.900
on screen it is Head
of Talent Acquisition.

13
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.540
Sign in with your DBL email and password.

14
00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:08.108
On Access Control, as the admin sees it,
your row carries Head of Talent

15
00:01:08.228 --> 00:01:11.971
Acquisition, Global, all units,
because the role covers every unit.

16
00:01:12.331 --> 00:01:18.090
Granting it takes a super user or the
admin login; you cannot grant it yourself.

17
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:23.840
Let us start with Approval Paths,
because without it nobody can raise a

18
00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:28.800
requisition at all. Per unit,
you decide here who may raise,

19
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.660
and whose desks their requisition crosses.

20
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.080
Not set up means nobody yet in that unit.

21
00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:41.630
Add a raiser. The unit, the department,
then the person from the directory.

22
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:46.190
Notice: naming them creates their access;

23
00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.190
nothing to do separately
on Access Control.

24
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.580
Now their chain.
Search an approver, Add approval step,

25
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.940
give it a label, say Unit Head.
Another one, SBU Head.

26
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.540
The two arrows, Move up
and Move down, set the order.

27
00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.860
Two raisers in the same unit
can have different chains.

28
00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:14.136
One step sits at the bottom by itself,
yours: Head of Talent Acquisition,

29
00:02:14.256 --> 00:02:18.874
always last, the final approval.
It cannot be removed.

30
00:02:18.994 --> 00:02:24.249
Save chain.
A chain with no other steps works too;

31
00:02:24.369 --> 00:02:28.130
the requisition
then comes straight to you.

32
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.720
A few rules. A raiser cannot be their
own approver; the save refuses it.

33
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.880
No chain means no raising. And the chain
is copied when a requisition is raised;

34
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.960
changing it later does
not reroute one in flight.

35
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:48.550
If someone on Access Control carries
an amber No approval path chip,

36
00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:53.630
they hold the role but have no chain. They
cannot raise; come here and build one.

37
00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:59.060
You end every chain. When one arrives,
the Approvals tab shows four buttons:

38
00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:04.260
Approve, Need more info,
Reject, and Send to CHRO.

39
00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.100
The first three work as for any approver.

40
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.770
Like any approver, check Details,
Job Analysis and the facilities first.

41
00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:18.690
Then Approve. Status Approved;
the raiser and Factory HR are told.

42
00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.530
From here,
launching recruitment is your job.

43
00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:27.160
Send to CHRO is for when
the decision should go up.

44
00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.640
Click it and a CHRO level is appended
to the chain and the CHRO is told.

45
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.480
Their part is in Role Guide 05.

46
00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:41.070
Two things. In a unit with no Factory HR,
or everyone on leave,

47
00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:45.150
the job analysis comes to you
and the recruiters. And

48
00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:50.950
at any time you can correct a requisition
with Edit details; it is logged.

49
00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.460
Once a requisition is
Approved you have three jobs,

50
00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.340
all on the Profile & Posting tab.

51
00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:02.460
First, CV collection sources:
LinkedIn, BDJobs, career site, campus,

52
00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:08.420
referral, wherever CVs will come from.
Tick them, Save sources.

53
00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:11.040
Second, Assign recruiter.

54
00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:16.970
Until the sources are saved, the panel
asks you to save them first, look.

55
00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:22.250
Once saved, pick one from
the Corporate Recruiters,

56
00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.410
here Ishrat Jahan.

57
00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.930
From now on everything downstream
is theirs; your access remains.

58
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.840
Third, the role profile.

59
00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.920
A draft is already there from
Factory HR's job analysis.

60
00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.120
Use this profile keeps it,

61
00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.640
Regenerate asks the AI to write it afresh,
Edit lets you change it yourself.

62
00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.561
Set the application closing date,
Publish job posting.

63
00:04:48.681 --> 00:04:54.817
Status Posted, the job is on the careers
page, the Drive folders are created.

64
00:04:54.937 --> 00:04:58.196
Share job link sends the link;

65
00:04:58.316 --> 00:05:02.070
Social post gives a ready Facebook post.

66
00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.190
Often the recruiter does this;
either of you can.

67
00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.980
A small job people forget.

68
00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:14.660
The requisition's facility requirements,
laptop, transport,

69
00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:20.332
dormitory: confirm them on Details,
or skip what cannot be given.

70
00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:25.060
Transport and dormitory, when asked for,
carry a caveat on purpose:

71
00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:30.860
they are never guaranteed, they
depend on the route and on allocation.

72
00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:36.610
Candidates lists every posted requisition,
one click into any pipeline.

73
00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:42.186
Talent Bank holds every past finalist;
search, then Add to Requisition Pipeline.

74
00:05:42.306 --> 00:05:46.810
Whatever the recruiter can do,
you can; Role Guide 07 has all of it.

75
00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.280
Now Hiring Approval Sheets.
When a recruiter clicks Send for

76
00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:56.560
Board Approval on a candidate, it lands
on Approval Sheets, under Waiting on you.

77
00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.030
This is DBL's twelve-column
paper form, digital.

78
00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:04.510
Tick one or more candidates
and send them on one sheet.

79
00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:09.290
Education, experience
and last employer come from the CV;

80
00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:12.060
fix anything wrong in the send dialog,
before sending.

81
00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.540
Pick the CHRO, here Dr. Kamrul Hassan.

82
00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:21.500
Then the board members,
from your Board Groups. Send sheet.

83
00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:27.300
The sheet gets an HAS number, everyone
is emailed, the links last sixty days.

84
00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:33.210
Under Sheets you have sent,
the progress: the CHRO, then the board.

85
00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:39.370
No answer from someone,
Resend sends fresh links only to them.

86
00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:44.290
Download it as Excel,
with the CV links, or print.

87
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:50.760
Each sent sheet shows its trail
beneath it: who decided what,

88
00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:55.347
and who is still to answer.
When the board approves,

89
00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:59.360
each candidate's Board Approval step
in onboarding completes by itself.

90
00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.230
Medical Requests. When a recruiter
asks for a medical test it lands here,

91
00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:08.310
undated. You set each candidate's date,

92
00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:12.350
time and venue, or tick several
and apply one to all.

93
00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:17.780
Who receives it: the medical team,
the candidate, or both.

94
00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:24.620
Send. One email per candidate.
Role Guide 10 has the medical team's side.

95
00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:28.820
The medical team's letter lists the
candidate's tests, the set for below forty

96
00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:34.130
or for forty and above, the reference
number, the date and the venue.

97
00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:40.730
The candidate's appointment says only when
and where to come. Both are in your name.

98
00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:47.210
A few settings are yours. AI Settings:
the shortlist threshold, Lenient,

99
00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:53.040
Balanced, Strict. Whether new CVs
are screened automatically. Whether

100
00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:59.681
a role profile is drafted on approval.
And the pass marks for the three tests.

101
00:08:00.261 --> 00:08:03.341
Board Groups: named sets of board members,

102
00:08:03.461 --> 00:08:06.701
so sending a sheet brings
them all in one click.

103
00:08:07.621 --> 00:08:10.421
New group, add members, save.

104
00:08:10.771 --> 00:08:13.913
AI Proficiency Bank: questions by grade.

105
00:08:14.033 --> 00:08:17.963
Generate with AI brings a batch of drafts;

106
00:08:18.083 --> 00:08:23.491
only what you keep after reading is saved.
Edit them, delete in bulk.

107
00:08:23.841 --> 00:08:30.281
Unit Config: units, departments and seats,
how many sanctioned, how many filled.

108
00:08:31.201 --> 00:08:35.321
This is what decides New versus
Replacement on a requisition,

109
00:08:35.441 --> 00:08:37.761
so keep the organogram right.

110
00:08:38.111 --> 00:08:42.891
You are told when:
a requisition awaits your final approval,

111
00:08:43.011 --> 00:08:47.871
a job analysis falls to you,
a candidate awaits a sheet,

112
00:08:47.991 --> 00:08:53.151
a medical test needs scheduling,
and IT creates someone's email.

113
00:08:53.501 --> 00:08:56.581
Questions.
Why can I not assign a recruiter?

114
00:08:57.421 --> 00:09:02.021
The CV sources are not saved.
A raiser cannot raise?

115
00:09:02.861 --> 00:09:06.741
Look for No approval path beside
their name on Access Control,

116
00:09:06.861 --> 00:09:08.761
and build the chain in Approval Paths.

117
00:09:08.891 --> 00:09:13.451
In short. Raisers
and chains in Approval Paths.

118
00:09:13.571 --> 00:09:16.692
On the last level, Approve
or Send to CHRO. Once Approved:

119
00:09:17.132 --> 00:09:22.052
sources, recruiter, profile, publish. Send
sheets to the board from Approval Sheets.

120
00:09:22.172 --> 00:09:27.093
Date the tests in Medical Requests.

121
00:09:27.692 --> 00:09:32.251
The full guide is a PDF under Tutorials.
Thank you.

